ummary type="html">Haiti's Prime Minister congratulating El Salvador's President for a gang crackdown in Haiti has shone a light on the relationship between the two countries. What's going on, and where does the US stand?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran targeted US radar system in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb1a85a9c927dfc7b0ab3fc25c2bf5c338f9ff2df8ed7e103dcbfda9d41eebe8</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640--6a6890129eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran claimed it struck US radar systems in Bahrain, while the US said it had intercepted the attacks. Clashes continue in the Strait of Hormuz, as the war remains in a state of de-escalation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing faces its Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39af6be7acbaf68465d50bf9290a800f9dd639296cfbdd6f0892e14a9c6659e0</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--4d68b234d525.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Moscow, Beijing is risking its image at the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cyber attacks and hybrid warfare: Germany gives sweeping powers to its police and intelligence services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d274ea786678fcac968e19bd2a9f6c02d7bd5b6cb21b215f609c081f380b55c</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-servic/a-79941507--8b38eb9f8681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-services/a-79941507?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone sightings and cyberattacks have heightened security concerns. How are the police preparing to meet these challenges? And how do intelligence services plan to counter threats from both domestic and foreign sources?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens a political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f888db3ec8a2a3b3cf42d4c824fdc494c8812c56b2c4be2d537625c577bbb21</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753--0451bf449bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64ea71601b741faa16f123988b9f2f832d61576b44a609a94a7962a7cfb90ad1</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms has cast doubt on Anthropic's looming IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed70624bc63bbe5702de7c6c3bf70b5f1739fead46dff66390d618dbec307f98</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:34:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp says that midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders gather for first ever AI summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e11d9b387b9398ecc9c2e783c6f8371defe410060a239c43fa7280b1db4ba473</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-gather-for-first-ever-ai-summit/a-79937463--f8be7038ec58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-gather-for-first-ever-ai-summit/a-79937463?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summit came as worries about the artificial intelligence's global impact mount and Europe seeks a role in its development and regulation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Russia hit with second car bomb attack in two days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04f0f3da6c8215db6f3a79250e55c25fc62853be9f8a86064dc0c5fba5d72925</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russia-hit-with-second-car-bomb-attack-in-two-days/live-79937459--6f8172d28fb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russia-hit-with-second-car-bomb-attack-in-two-days/live-79937459?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A second car bomb in two days exploded in Moscow, targeting an exiled Ukrainian political aide, according to Russian media. Meanwhile, Ukraine and Russia exchanged deadly strikes overnight. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Humanitarian situation in Gaza worsens amid political deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d5b2aaaaae027508df210ce1c4fad76715c28de0a278b79eedd10ef8035cfa3</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/humanitarian-situation-in-gaza-worsens-amid-political-deadlock/a-79931403--a8a6020c54fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/humanitarian-situation-in-gaza-worsens-amid-political-deadlock/a-79931403?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In war-battered Gaza, heavy rain flooded and damaged thousands of tents. Several people died. Could pressure by Trump's Board of Peace on Israel and Hamas help to ease the humanitarian crisis amid stalled peace talks?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament agrees on debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2435926974bd0d7500aaf3740c9aed05ad5c9a2eb03c2b66295cc5f2be11ae8b</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897--be62c4ec3578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget committee in the Bundestag worked into the night to sign off on next year's spending plans. These include levels of new debt only eclipsed once, at the height of the COVID pandemic. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest against cuts to public media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cee40019b0aac57b584d9bc1d39a3849df813a0b776c667935f247a49c0baf09</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-cuts-to-public-media/a-79933533--8665bbfc8f3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-cuts-to-public-media/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill to cut public media funding has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is planned for Prague on Sunday.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>After suffering its worst election result, what's next for the ANC — and for South Africa?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a3a2fe2a4f43ac4a429d5133aefaace7eeca411577494eb2f783cab57066ada</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-suffering-its-worst-election-result-what-s-next-for-the-anc-and-for-south-africa/a-79929902--0f5fc83270ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-suffering-its-worst-election-result-what-s-next-for-the-anc-and-for-south-africa/a-79929902?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A crushing local election result across the country has left South Africa's ruling ANC searching for answers. Experts say the vote reflects public frustration with service delivery failures — signaling a political shift.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aef3498d6e8a67ab2a12d4d518023b546eb9a95bf930498534a79a2078eac5fa</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>US Senate asks Huang, Lutnick to testify on Nvidia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70c347329db4b458b57c0118420b93613dcd7786fc9f03cff744c78c1021c68b</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-senate-asks-huang-lutnick-to-testify-on-nvidia/a-79936707--4c59d27e1ef4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-senate-asks-huang-lutnick-to-testify-on-nvidia/a-79936707?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senate Banking Committee Chairman Tim Scott has asked Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick and former Nvidia chief Jensen Huang to testify, as House Republicans demand closed-door interviews amid national security concerns.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian activist and Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi shares her story in memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbd25dd9045d2a3930d2810d2ae4b30cbccd23944c5b18908ba550e171e63046</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167--a983bd7e2dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Written and smuggled out of prison, the 2023 Nobel Prize laureate's memoir reveals the cost of defying Iran's regime and fighting for freedom.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Microsoft rules out 'malicious activity' as cause for global outage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfdc8bedd19db4e3a741c0006b804225c5225236182df44e091c9690b2ffa342</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T07:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/microsoft-rules-out-malicious-activity-as-cause-for-global-outage/a-79935611--12aa5f682eb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/microsoft-rules-out-malicious-activity-as-cause-for-global-outage/a-79935611?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Microsoft outage disrupted Outlook and Teams worldwide, with reports from scores of countries and territories. The software giant said that it was "not aware" of malicious activity that could have caused the outage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Sonam Wangchuk says he is under house arrest in Ladakh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3a7c15c02cf1a22df3351be43a4e9f1858103e22041469151df11263988a315</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:35:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T07:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-sonam-wangchuk-says-he-is-under-house-arrest-in-ladakh/live-79936475--47fb6447cba6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-sonam-wangchuk-says-he-is-under-house-arrest-in-ladakh/live-79936475?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Wangchuk is among activists in Ladakh who have raised concerns about upcoming regional elections, which they say are designed to diminish voter participation as they will be held in the harsh winter period. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US disrupts North Korea's $400 million crypto scam, FBI says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48b16020fa58201afdbf4860d0d184da33e286557b7b84910c0891e4d3df6eae</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:33:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T04:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-disrupts-north-korea-s-400-million-crypto-scam-fbi-says/a-79935957--ed83d7896a38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-disrupts-north-korea-s-400-million-crypto-scam-fbi-says/a-79935957?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has seized servers linked to a North Korean scam that used fake video meetings and deepfakes to steal more than $400 million in crypto, and has moved to seize $1.2 billion that was taken from Binance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Darth Vader strikes back at auction as his lightsaber from two original Star Wars films reclaims the record from Luke Skywalker's prop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3b92700e05b75ef9fe6a97c68fd536b83b90f6dfe674039733b84f825e24278</id><updated>2026-11-13T16:33:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T02:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/darth-vader-strikes-back-at-auction-as-his-lightsaber-from-two-original-star-wars-films-reclaims-the/a-79935960--81f69e9d2499.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/darth-vader-strikes-back-at-auction-as-his-lightsaber-from-two-original-star-wars-films-reclaims-the-record-from-luke-skywalker-s-prop/a-79935960?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Darth Vader's lightsaber sold for nearly $5 million, breaking the record set by Luke Skywalker's in July. The hilt, made from a 1950s camera flash attachment, was used in two of the original trilogy's duels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
